<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We vary the number of LoRA-inserted layers (0, 4, 8, 10, 12). The largest gain is from 0<math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!\to\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!\to\!</annotation></semantics></math>8 layers (C: +12.9, B4: +3.3, M: +2.9, R: +5.7). With 10 layers, accuracy peaks (C = 87.05), while 8 layers yields the best language metrics (B4/M/R).
12 layers cause worse results, indicating mild overfitting.
8-10 layers offers the best trade-off between QA accuracy and text quality.
We use #Layers = 8 to balance computation and accuracy.</p>
</div>
</section>
