<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#S6.T7" title="In F.2 SFC curve count ‣ F Additional results ‣ Efficient Encoder-Free Fourier-based 3D Large Multimodal Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, performance on ScanQA improves as the number of SFC curves increases, but largely saturates from <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{C}{=}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{C}{=}4</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> with only marginal gains. We therefore set <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{C}{=}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{C}{=}4</annotation></semantics></math> to balance accuracy and computational cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
